Third-party components
----------------------

None. Voice has no third-party dependency and no CDN.

Vendored from this project's own kits (same licence, same author), copied verbatim on
25/11/2026:

- web-kit 0.1.0 — docs/play/web-kit.js — the offline shell, storage helpers and PWA registration
- export-kit 1.0.0 — docs/play/export-kit.js — Blob download, used to write the memoir and save a clip

Neither kit is modified. Neither makes a network request.

On transcription and models
---------------------------

The Griot prompt asks for on-device speech-to-text and a bring-your-own-key LLM; the Mimic prompt
asks for an LLM that writes in your voice. There is no speech model and no language model in this
app: the recording is kept and played while the words are typed, the questions are a bundled bank,
and a draft is written by measured rules. The voice card's numbers are computed from the samples
the person supplied, and nothing about a voice is asserted that was not measured from them.
